get_worker_trace:
View the [execution process] of an intent (work) (unlike get_worker_output, which gives only the final conclusion). Three usages:
① intent_id only → returns the summary stream of each step of the work (summary ≤100 chars, with step_id; only an outline of the actions, not the full output);
② intent_id + q → returns only the step summaries matching the keyword (searches both summaries and full outputs; still gives only summaries — use ③ to see content);
③ intent_id + step_ids → returns the full content (detail) of those steps; at most 5 per call — beyond that only the first 5 are returned and the ones not fetched are reported in notice/omitted_step_ids.
Typical flow: first locate suspicious steps' step_ids with ①/②, then fetch their full output with ③. Thinking steps are not included. Historical traces of directly related tasks are supported; their results carry source_task_id/inherited=true and are read-only.
